From dc02297df5ab97f4bfd87236fae9ce9bdb42760d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: root <root@MyComputer.localdomain>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 20:49:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 34/38] perf(spec): port upstream #35544 GDN ReplaySSM
 checkpoint amortization
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces per-verify-step full checkpoint materialization with a bounded
circular history: one materialization per accepted verify window, taken
off the decode critical path. Upstream merged 2026-09-04 (db89f639ef),
Base CI green, nine targeted GPU accuracy tests upstream.

Port notes:
- 8 files three-way merged onto our tree (replayssm kernel, memory_pool,
  spec_utils, kv_cache_configurator, mamba_utils, gdn_backend,
  attention_hook, mamba_radix_cache).
- #37837 ReplaySSM ring-cursor reset on the extra_buffer donate path
  re-grafted onto the refactored donate_mamba_ping_pong_slot.
- Upstream MLA DCP-sharded scatter reference neutralized (DeepSeek MLA
  feature from another PR; write_loc_is_dcp_resolved is False on this
  stack) — plain triton scatter covers every reachable case.
- async_probe.py taken wholesale from upstream (adds
  maybe_detect_kernel_facing_loc / maybe_detect_in_closed_range needed
  by the new memory_pool and spec_utils).
- Our BACKUP-ON-EVICT, attribution logs and audit heartbeat live in
  mamba_component.py/unified_tree_core.py — untouched by this port.
